Students who opt to enroll in BIOL 490 Honors Thesis Research and BIOL 491 Honors Thesis will require permission of the course coordinator and must have a cGPA of at least 3.25 at the end of the sixth semester of the third academic year, a B or above in BIOL 355 Critical Research Reasoning and have secured a project and supervisor. These students must successfully:
complete the progress review as part of BIOL 490 Honors Thesis Research at the end of the Fall semester of the fourth year, respectively, in the form of a progress report;
conduct the necessary research towards the completion of BIOL 490 Honors Thesis Research;
write the Honors Thesis (BIOL 491) according to the Department’s B.Sc. Thesis Format and Style Guidelines;
obtain approval of the Honors Thesis the supervisor and advisory committee;
pass the thesis defense. A “revise” decision is not a “pass” and only one revision is permitted

6 credits of Theory (Anthropology of Performance OR Postcolonial Theory and its Applications in Eurasia OR Classical Sociological Theory); 
At least one course at the intermediate or advanced level in any subfield
12 ECTS
